  "title": "CMake: Set Python3_FIND_REGISTRY NEVER on MSYS2",
  "description": "On Windows, by default, CMake FindPython3 will prefer Python\ninstalled in locations mentioned in the registry in to locations\nmentioned in PATH and other relevant environment variables.\nOn MSYS2, the PATH is set up to properly contain the correct\nPython3 and we never want to use Python mentioned in the registry.\n\nDo that and we can use FindPython3 instead of the deprecated\nFindPythonInterp (which is removed by CMP0148, new in CMake 3.27).\n\nThis requires CMake 3.13, which is already our minimum.\n\nSee https://gitlab.kitware.com/cmake/cmake/-/issues/21658",
  "state": "merged",
